description: Testing strategy and error-handling conventions
globs: "{apps,modules,packages}/**/*.{ts,tsx}"
alwaysApply: false
---

# Testing

- Unit-test domain rules, pricing, and state machines next to code (`*.spec.ts`)
- Integration-test API + DB + RLS for persistence/HTTP (`*.integration.spec.ts`)
- Every new tenant-scoped API/table needs a cross-tenant isolation test
- Commercial paths (quotes, orders, inventory, authz) require automated tests before merge
- Shared factories live in `packages/testing`

# Errors

- Map domain errors to stable API codes (`quote.expired`, `order.invalid_transition`)
- AuthZ fail closed; no empty catches; sanitize `500` messages
- Honor `Idempotency-Key` on quote/order/payment/stock movement creates
- Prefer explicit transition endpoints over free-form status patches
